          "text": "The pattern is best indexed as an orthorhombic **TiNiSi-type** phase, space group **Pnma (No. 62)**, with \\(Z=4\\). The approximate cell is \\(a=7.577\\), \\(b=3.792\\), \\(c=7.586\\) \u00c5. The near relationships \\(a\\approx c\\approx2b\\) produce the pronounced pseudo-cubic peak grouping and several unresolved overlaps.\n\nThe carbon coordinates are intrinsically less well constrained by Cu X-ray data; the coordinates below should therefore be regarded as a starting model for Rietveld refinement rather than a final high-precision determination.\n\n```cif\ndata_YbCdC\n_audit_creation_method\n;Powder indexing and TiNiSi-type constrained structure solution\n from Cu Kalpha diffraction data\n;\n_chemical_name_common                  'ytterbium cadmium carbide'\n_chemical_formula_sum                  'Yb Cd C'\n_chemical_formula_structural           'YbCdC'\n_cell_formula_units_Z                   4\n\n_cell_length_a                          7.577\n_cell_length_b                          3.792\n_cell_length_c                          7.586\n_cell_angle_alpha                       90\n_cell_angle_beta                        90\n_cell_angle_gamma                       90\n_cell_volume                            217.96\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt               'P n m a'\n_space_group_IT_number                  62\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn           9.07\n_diffrn_radiation_type                  'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength            1.5406\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '1/2-x,-y,1/2+z'\n3  '-x,1/2+y,-z'\n4  '1/2+x,1/2-y,1/2-z'\n5  '-x,-y,-z'\n6  '1/2+x,y,1/2-z'\n7  'x,1/2-y,z'\n8  '1/2-x,1/2+y,1/2+z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nYb1  Yb  4  c  0.0200  0.2500  0.6840  1.0  0.006\nCd1  Cd  4  c  0.1780  0.2500  0.0580  1.0  0.008\nC1   C   4  c  0.2880  0.2500  0.3880  1.0  0.010\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing is approximately:\n\n| 2\u03b8 observed | Principal reflection group |\n|---:|:---|\n| 23.52\u00b0 | 200/002 |\n| 28.8\u00b0 | 111 |\n| 33.34\u00b0 | 210/012/202 |\n| 37.49\u00b0 | 301/103 |\n| 41.20\u00b0 | 212 |\n| 44.60\u00b0 | 311/113 |\n| 48.10\u00b0 | 400/020/004 |\n| 57.02\u00b0 | 313-type group |\n| 62.28\u00b0 | 501/105 and nearby overlaps |\n| 67.5\u201367.7\u00b0 | 511/115-related group |\n\nThe main residual ambiguity is a pseudo-tetragonal body-centered indexing with a cell near \\(7.58\\times7.58\\) \u00c5. It accounts well for peak positions but does not provide as chemically or crystallographically economical a complete YbCdC model as the Pnma, \\(Z=4\\), TiNiSi-type solution.",
